<li>Ronald Fagin, <a href="https://research.ibm.com/publications/multivalued-dependencies-and-a-new-normal-form-for-relational-databases">Multivalued Dependencies and a New Normal Form for Relational Databases</a> (1977): multivalued dependencies and fourth normal form.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/ddl-constraints.html">Constraints</a>: primary keys, composite uniqueness, required values and references. The site’s <a href="https://staycurrent.dev/learn/databases/relational/constraints/">Constraints</a> article develops their practical enforcement.</li>
<li>PostgreSQL 18, <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/datatype-json.html#JSON-DOC-DESIGN">Designing JSON Documents</a>: keeping document structure meaningful alongside relational data. <a href="https://staycurrent.dev/learn/databases/relational/values/">Values</a> covers value representation, types and missing data.</li>
<li>On this site: <a href="https://staycurrent.dev/learn/databases/relational/data-lifecycle/">Data lifecycle</a> for historical facts and corrections, <a href="https://staycurrent.dev/learn/databases/relational/transaction-boundaries/">Transactions</a> for related writes, and <a href="https://staycurrent.dev/learn/databases/relational/indexes/">Indexes</a> for physical read costs.</li>
</ul>
